      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A commentary on the problem of tolerance to opioids is presented from the perspective of a person with chronic nonmalignant pain. The writer challenges the position of many clinicians and professional societies that tolerance to opioid analgesia usually is not a barrier to effective pain management. Implications for clinicians are presented."},
